{
  "an7.19:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 7.19 ",
  "an7.19:0.2": "2. Tendencies ",
  "an7.19:0.3": "Extinguishment ",
  "an7.19:1.1": "“One meditates observing the happiness in extinguishment. They perceive happiness and experience happiness. Constantly, continually, and without interruption, they apply the mind and fathom with wisdom. ",
  "an7.19:1.2": "They’ve realized the undefiled freedom of heart and freedom by wisdom, and live having realized it with their own insight in this very life due to the ending of defilements. ",
  "an7.19:1.3": "This is the first individual worthy of offerings. ",
  "an7.19:2.1": "Next, take an individual who meditates observing the happiness in extinguishment. They perceive happiness and experience happiness. Constantly, continually, and without interruption, they apply the mind and fathom with wisdom. ",
  "an7.19:2.2": "Their defilements and their life come to an end at exactly the same time. ",
  "an7.19:2.3": "This is the second individual. ",
  "an7.19:3.1": "Next, take an individual who meditates observing the happiness in extinguishment. They perceive happiness and experience happiness. Constantly, continually, and without interruption, they apply the mind and fathom with wisdom. ",
  "an7.19:3.2": "With the ending of the five lower fetters they’re extinguished between one life and the next. … ",
  "an7.19:3.3": "With the ending of the five lower fetters they’re extinguished upon landing. … ",
  "an7.19:3.4": "With the ending of the five lower fetters they’r